  "metadata": {
    "name": "toplevel_ref_metaparameter_axis",
    "description": "Conformance pin for the \u00a74.7 edge pipeline at a top-level models.<k> {ref}. Mounts toplevel_ref_metaparameter_axis_lib.esm, whose only axis is sized by the LEAF's own metaparameter (NLEV, default 4). \u00a74.7 \"Two mount forms, one mechanism\" forbids the two attachment points from differing, and the edge pipeline's step (1) resolves the referenced document in its OWN scope, so the leaf's metaparameters close and fold AT THE MOUNT (\u00a79.7.6 site 3) and `lev` reaches the importing registry as size 4 \u2014 the importer redeclares nothing, which is \u00a79.7.5's \"without redeclaring them\". All five bindings mount a top-level {ref} through the same edge pipeline they run at a `subsystems.<k>` edge, so the valid corpus sweep holds every one of them to this outcome.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciAST"],
    "created": "2026-09-07T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": ["subsystem", "index_sets", "metaparameter", "mount", "toplevel-ref", "regression"]
  },
